(FUN-42 — (gap) LANGUAGE.md never says WHERE a function definition may
 stand. The compiler accepts one nested inside an `If` body and inside a
 `While` body, and HOISTS it: the body does not run when the block runs,
 and the name is callable from the top level afterwards. The generator
 currently forbids this to itself (src/gen_flow.vox:495-501 says "a
 function definition is only legal at the top level"), which is safe but
 stricter than the language — and being stricter than the language is
 exactly the kind of undeclared rule CLAUDE.md is about. Note the output:
 "nested in an If" and "nested in a While" appear only where they are
 CALLED, not where the blocks execute.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FUN-42.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   blocks have run
   nested in an If
   nested in a While
)
a number called g is 1.
If g is 1 then,
  To 'from an if'.
    Print "nested in an If".

a number called rounds is 0.
While rounds is less than 1,
  Set rounds to rounds add 1,
  To 'from a while'.
    Print "nested in a While".

Print "blocks have run".
'from an if'.
'from a while'.
